{#-
  The ratings widget (SPEC §12): "Was this helpful?", five stars and a
  status line. It ends the row of controls of the video template, after
  "Audio only" and the handout (partials/video-block.njk, which renders it
  only while site.features.ratings is exactly true), so templates don't call
  it themselves:

    {% from "partials/rating.njk" import rating %}
    {{ rating(video) }}

  src/js/rating.js makes it work; the layouts load it only while
  site.features.ratings is exactly true.

  It ships `hidden`: without JavaScript there is nothing to show (a form
  POST can't reach the API, which takes JSON), and rating.js reveals it once
  it is listening.

  The root <div> is `display: contents` (components.css), so its two parts
  are items of the row: a <fieldset> whose legend is "Was this helpful?"
  plus the video's title for screen readers (a problem page has up to
  seven), with five native radios ("1 star" to "5 stars"; arrow keys move
  between them, and autocomplete="off" so a browser doesn't restore an old
  choice), each <label> a 44x44px star; then the status line, on its own
  line under the row, empty until there is news (decision a2 = B), its
  height reserved by hidden copies of the longest messages so the answer
  never shifts the page. Nothing else: no notice (project lead,
  2026-11-06, SPEC §15.1). `data-rating` names the video: pages.json reads
  it (SPEC §8.3), and rating.js sends it. ids are unique per page: the
  validator allows each video once per page.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- macro rating(video) -%}
{%- set id = video.video_id -%}
<div class="rating" data-rating="{{ id }}" hidden>
  <fieldset class="rating__group">
    <legend class="rating__legend">Was this helpful?<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ video.title }}</span></legend>
    <div class="rating__stars">
      {%- for n in range(1, 6) %}
      <input class="rating__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="rating-{{ id }}" id="rating-{{ id }}-{{ n }}" value="{{ n }}" autocomplete="off">
      <label class="rating__star" for="rating-{{ id }}-{{ n }}">{{ icon('star', 26, 'rating__icon') }}<span class="visually-hidden">{{ n }} star{{ 's' if n > 1 }}</span></label>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <div class="rating__status-box">
    <p class="rating__status" id="rating-{{ id }}-status" data-rating-status></p>
    <p class="rating__sizer" aria-hidden="true">Thanks. You rated this 5 of 5.</p>
    <p class="rating__sizer" aria-hidden="true">Couldn't send right now — please try again later</p>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
